WEBVTT

00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:19.733
<i>What's this feeling I have,</i>
<i>as if I'm looking forward to...</i>

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:25.939
<i>... somebody firing off his</i>
<i>missiles and ending everything?</i>

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:31.378
<i>Is it a bad thing, or is this normal?</i>

00:00:31.378 --> 00:00:37.884
<i>I can't figure it out on my</i>
<i>own, so somebody tell me!</i>

00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:43.490
<i>And that person I love has once again...</i>

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:49.930
<i>... gone far away without anybody noticing.</i>

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:56.103
<i>Where have my dreams gone since then?</i>

00:00:56.103 --> 00:01:01.775
<i>I could swear that they</i>
<i>were right here long ago.</i>

00:01:01.775 --> 00:01:07.814
<i>We had a love that set our hearts on fire.</i>

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:20.784
<i>Let's take back that feeling we had back then!</i>

00:01:54.961 --> 00:01:58.598
This is the Manuketa Comet,
a twin comet which is currently

00:01:58.598 --> 00:02:00.367
approaching Earth once again.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:03.303
It is named for a
Mr. Manuketa of Mie Prefecture,

00:02:03.303 --> 00:02:07.007
an astronomy buff who
first discovered the comet.

00:02:07.007 --> 00:02:10.510
This is no time to be sitting
around watching television!

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:12.307
A-Ayeka!

00:02:18.452 --> 00:02:21.688
It can't be good for us
to just leave things be!

00:02:21.688 --> 00:02:23.757
Am I right, everyone?!

00:02:23.757 --> 00:02:24.758
Leave what be?

00:02:24.758 --> 00:02:26.426
What else could I be talking about?!

00:02:26.426 --> 00:02:31.331
Lord Tenchi's impure
dalliance with that "Sakuya" woman!

00:02:31.331 --> 00:02:36.036
We've had to put it off because of
the attack of that strange girl, Yugi,

00:02:36.036 --> 00:02:39.272
but now is the time to find
out the truth once and for all!

00:02:39.272 --> 00:02:41.708
How do we do that?

00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:45.545
We go to Tokyo and ask
Lord Tenchi directly, of course!

00:02:45.545 --> 00:02:47.948
You mean, use the Dimension Tunnel
again and drop in unannounced?

00:02:47.948 --> 00:02:50.317
Oh, the Dimension Tunnel's broken.

00:02:50.317 --> 00:02:52.285
It'll take until this evening to fix it.

00:02:52.285 --> 00:02:53.653
What?!

00:02:53.653 --> 00:02:57.190
L-In that case, we'll have Father,
the cause of this problem,

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:59.426
give us money, and
we'll take the bullet train!

00:02:59.426 --> 00:03:01.428
Nobuyuki isn't here.

00:03:01.428 --> 00:03:03.163
What?

00:03:03.163 --> 00:03:05.632
I found this when I woke up this morning.

00:03:05.632 --> 00:03:09.534
"I'm leaving on a trip. Please
don't look for me. Nobuyuki."

00:03:09.836 --> 00:03:12.472
So he's chickened out, has he?!

00:03:12.472 --> 00:03:16.476
In that case, make a flying
mecha in three seconds, Washu!

00:03:16.476 --> 00:03:19.546
Sorry, but I'm not in the mood right now.

00:03:19.546 --> 00:03:21.414
There are some things I want to look into.

00:03:21.414 --> 00:03:25.285
I have to figure out the gems'
power before we face that girl again.

00:03:25.285 --> 00:03:27.254
Washu!

00:03:27.254 --> 00:03:29.456
Mihoshi, it's time for our patrol.

00:03:29.456 --> 00:03:30.690
We're really going?

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:34.761
Of course! We're Galaxy
Police detectives, remember?

00:03:34.761 --> 00:03:36.029
Kiyone!

00:03:36.029 --> 00:03:39.165
I'm sorry. We have a job to do.

00:03:39.165 --> 00:03:41.468
Wait for me, Kiyone!

00:03:41.468 --> 00:03:46.406
I have no choice, Ryoko. I'd rather
not, but we have to work together.

00:03:46.406 --> 00:03:48.108
Ryoko!

00:03:48.108 --> 00:03:49.876
I'm not going, either.

00:03:49.876 --> 00:03:51.611
Ryoko...

00:03:51.611 --> 00:03:53.272
I...

00:04:06.393 --> 00:04:09.195
I have faith in Tenchi.

00:04:09.195 --> 00:04:10.864
Ryoko...

00:04:10.864 --> 00:04:12.866
Even Ryoko?

00:04:12.866 --> 00:04:17.200
Very well, then, I'll make it to
Tokyo no matter what it takes!

00:04:18.605 --> 00:04:20.740
And go to Lord Tenchi's side!

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.367
"Ah!" "Uh oh!"

00:04:22.842 --> 00:04:24.678
But with no money or transportation,
how in the world can I get there?

00:04:24.678 --> 00:04:26.947
"Money" "Vehicle"
But with no money or transportation,
how in the world can I get there?

00:04:26.947 --> 00:04:28.081
But with no money or transportation,
how in the world can I get there?

00:04:28.081 --> 00:04:30.675
Are you okay, Ryo-Ohki?

00:04:32.919 --> 00:04:34.588
Sasami!

00:04:34.588 --> 00:04:38.158
Ryo-Ohki is feeling sick today, so forget it!

00:04:38.158 --> 00:04:39.989
Oh, I see...

00:04:42.228 --> 00:04:44.664
And so, we're joined today
by Mr. Gantetsu Sarumoto,

00:04:44.664 --> 00:04:47.334
an adventurer who just
returned to Japan the other day.

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:51.171
Now, I'm told that you lost all
your money on your trip, Mr. Sarumoto.

00:04:51.171 --> 00:04:53.373
Yes, I was in a real pinch there.

00:04:53.373 --> 00:04:56.276
I managed to make my way by hitchhiking.

00:04:56.276 --> 00:05:00.178
I've never been as touched by the
compassion of others as I was then.

00:05:01.281 --> 00:05:03.183
Hitchhiking!

00:05:03.183 --> 00:05:06.987
Yes! I'll hitchhike there! That's it!

00:05:06.987 --> 00:05:10.445
Okay, this is the last room, Ryo-Ohki!

00:05:12.926 --> 00:05:14.227
Let's go, Sasami!

00:05:14.227 --> 00:05:15.595
W-Where?

00:05:15.595 --> 00:05:17.825
To Lord Tenchi's side!

00:05:26.706 --> 00:05:29.843
Maybe I'll take her to Tokyo.

00:05:29.843 --> 00:05:32.073
To Tokyo? What for?

00:05:34.247 --> 00:05:37.651
To show her this.

00:05:37.651 --> 00:05:39.753
This can shatter the ties that bind them...

00:05:39.753 --> 00:05:43.390
...far more effectively
than clumsy little pranks.

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:47.694
It sounds like there's still some
damage left from that fight earlier.

00:05:47.694 --> 00:05:49.195
Just leave it to me.

00:05:49.195 --> 00:05:52.699
Someone perfect for the job
will be in this planet's vicinity soon.

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:56.294
Let's use this. I know it'll be fun!

00:05:59.572 --> 00:06:01.474
Over here!

00:06:01.474 --> 00:06:01.675
"Tokyo"
Over here!

00:06:01.675 --> 00:06:04.644
"Tokyo"
Sister, this is so embarrassing!

00:06:04.644 --> 00:06:05.042
Sister, this is so embarrassing!

00:06:07.313 --> 00:06:08.948
Here comes one, Sasami!

00:06:08.948 --> 00:06:11.143
Over here!

00:06:17.924 --> 00:06:20.085
Over here!

00:06:25.865 --> 00:06:27.567
What's up? You're hitchhiking?

00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:32.197
Forget about that! Come
with us and we'll have some fun!

00:06:33.239 --> 00:06:34.831
How insolent!

00:06:35.675 --> 00:06:38.200
H-Help!

00:06:39.245 --> 00:06:41.372
Over here!

00:06:43.883 --> 00:06:45.783
- Forgive us!
- We're sorry!

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:49.352
Over here!

00:06:51.658 --> 00:06:54.127
There's a cutie out here waving to me!

00:06:54.127 --> 00:06:58.164
Hey, she'd make a perfect bride
young enough to be your granddaughter!

00:06:58.164 --> 00:07:00.600
Over here!

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.335
That'll never work.

00:07:02.335 --> 00:07:04.804
Nobody will give her a ride with that.

00:07:04.804 --> 00:07:09.002
You've gotta put more effort into it, lady!

00:07:11.177 --> 00:07:12.940
Little brats...

00:07:16.483 --> 00:07:19.686
Sister, it's hopeless...

00:07:19.686 --> 00:07:22.489
We'll never be able to hitchhike
all the way from Okayama to Tokyo.

00:07:22.489 --> 00:07:24.124
It's not hopeless!

00:07:24.124 --> 00:07:26.993
The strength of my love for Lord Tenchi

00:07:26.993 --> 00:07:30.292
would take me to
America or even to the moon!

00:07:31.731 --> 00:07:35.497
Sasami! Never give up!

00:07:47.313 --> 00:07:49.178
Tokyo, huh?

00:07:58.625 --> 00:08:00.456
"Cool"
"Very nice"

00:08:00.927 --> 00:08:02.095
Need a lift?

00:08:02.095 --> 00:08:07.233
Yes, but I have no money! Okay?

00:08:07.233 --> 00:08:08.568
Okay.

00:08:08.568 --> 00:08:10.236
Thank you!

00:08:10.236 --> 00:08:12.172
Yay!

00:08:12.172 --> 00:08:14.834
What's with the English all of a sudden?

00:08:17.043 --> 00:08:18.077
Let's roll!

00:08:18.077 --> 00:08:19.045
Ready!

00:08:19.045 --> 00:08:23.744
Please wait for me,
Lord Tenchi! I'm on my way!

00:08:28.521 --> 00:08:30.557
Okay, that's that.

00:08:30.557 --> 00:08:33.059
Huh? Where's the other one I made?

00:08:33.059 --> 00:08:34.651
Oh, well.

00:08:41.701 --> 00:08:45.762
Nobody's faster than Racer Joe's super bike!

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.133
Huh? What's that screaming?

00:08:52.645 --> 00:08:54.647
I lost! They blew my doors off!

00:08:54.647 --> 00:08:57.582
L-I'm getting dizzy!

00:08:58.518 --> 00:09:00.954
This bike is incredible!

00:09:00.954 --> 00:09:05.323
Nobody's wheels can stand up
to the bike of Speed Demon Ken!

00:09:09.429 --> 00:09:11.798
H-Help!

00:09:11.798 --> 00:09:14.200
At this rate, we'll be in Tokyo in no time!

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.862
Lord Tenchi, please wait for me!

00:09:25.879 --> 00:09:28.248
That's amazing!

00:09:28.248 --> 00:09:30.717
You're great at drawing, Masaki!

00:09:30.717 --> 00:09:33.253
I've liked drawing ever since I was little.

00:09:33.253 --> 00:09:35.755
Maybe it's my dad's influence.

00:09:35.755 --> 00:09:37.586
What is it?

00:09:38.858 --> 00:09:42.123
It's not finished yet...

00:09:45.131 --> 00:09:46.699
Uh... I guess so.

00:09:46.699 --> 00:09:48.724
Yeah.

00:09:56.976 --> 00:09:59.706
Faster! Faster! Go!

00:10:02.615 --> 00:10:04.674
Lord Tenchi!

00:10:19.933 --> 00:10:23.503
I'm always hungry...

00:10:23.503 --> 00:10:26.472
If you're looking for
Sasami, she left with Ayeka.

00:10:26.472 --> 00:10:28.007
Oh.

00:10:28.007 --> 00:10:32.011
Sorry, I don't feel like cooking
for anybody else right now.

00:10:32.011 --> 00:10:35.344
I'm going to eat in my room,
so make yourself at home.

00:10:36.749 --> 00:10:39.013
It's been a while, but I guess
I can cook something for myself.

00:10:44.657 --> 00:10:45.992
That hit the spot!

00:10:45.992 --> 00:10:50.396
I'm sorry. Now we've even
imposed on you for tea, um...

00:10:50.396 --> 00:10:52.799
Masayo. Masayo Manuketa.

00:10:52.799 --> 00:10:55.935
My name is Ayeka. This is my sister...

00:10:55.935 --> 00:10:57.870
Sasami!

00:10:57.870 --> 00:10:59.531
Why are you going to Tokyo?

00:11:02.008 --> 00:11:04.610
I'm glad you asked!

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:08.214
There are tears in the listening
and in the telling of this tale

00:11:08.214 --> 00:11:10.550
of long-distance romance
that is unfolding before me!

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:12.882
Here we go again...

00:11:14.821 --> 00:11:19.892
There is a gentleman with
whom I have pledged my future.

00:11:19.892 --> 00:11:24.130
His name is Tenchi Masaki.
In order to become a fine husband,

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:27.156
he left on a journey to Tokyo for training.

00:11:28.167 --> 00:11:33.973
But there in Tokyo, a stalker woman
named Sakuya was lying in wait for him!

00:11:33.973 --> 00:11:36.175
This stalker, Sakuya, seduced
Lord Tenchi with her diabolical powers

00:11:36.175 --> 00:11:37.844
"Gyaa!!"
This stalker, Sakuya, seduced
Lord Tenchi with her diabolical powers

00:11:37.844 --> 00:11:38.177
"Gyaa!!"
And spirited him away!

00:11:38.177 --> 00:11:40.113
And spirited him away!

00:11:40.113 --> 00:11:43.412
Oh, what is to become of my Lord Tenchi?!

00:11:45.151 --> 00:11:47.754
And so, I, as Lord Tenchi's
betrothed, am hitchhiking

00:11:47.754 --> 00:11:51.691
in order to save my future husband!

00:11:51.691 --> 00:11:53.192
Which is really a lie.

00:11:53.192 --> 00:11:57.163
She just wants to find out how this
guy she likes really feels about her.

00:11:57.163 --> 00:11:59.098
Right...

00:11:59.098 --> 00:12:02.668
To find out how a guy you like really feels...

00:12:02.668 --> 00:12:06.739
Oh, is there a man that
you're in love with, Masayo?

00:12:06.739 --> 00:12:11.744
Yeah. His name's Isao. Isao Ketauchi.

00:12:11.744 --> 00:12:14.280
He's the fastest man in the universe.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.682
Oh, now I understand, Masayo!

00:12:16.682 --> 00:12:20.686
To catch up with this fastest man in
the universe, you're traveling the country,

00:12:20.686 --> 00:12:23.189
constantly picking up hitchhikers!

00:12:23.189 --> 00:12:26.283
Sister, that's ridiculous!

00:12:27.393 --> 00:12:30.163
She's going into Delusion Mode again!

00:12:30.163 --> 00:12:34.700
Yes. It's a tale of high-speed love...

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:36.803
He's the fastest man in the universe.

00:12:36.803 --> 00:12:41.672
You couldn't catch this man,
who flew past everyone on the road...

00:12:44.877 --> 00:12:46.813
But you never gave up!

00:12:46.813 --> 00:12:51.951
You added a sidecar upgrade,
and now you can finally catch him!

00:12:51.951 --> 00:12:56.989
And now you're traveling the
country, searching for him, aren't you?

00:12:56.989 --> 00:13:00.126
Like that could ever happen!

00:13:00.126 --> 00:13:04.187
Oh, what a moving story!

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:10.767
Uh... M-Masayo?

00:13:19.679 --> 00:13:25.118
Thank you. You're the first
person who's ever understood me.

00:13:25.118 --> 00:13:26.452
Masayo...

00:13:26.452 --> 00:13:27.553
Ayeka...

00:13:27.553 --> 00:13:28.488
Masayo!

00:13:28.488 --> 00:13:29.188
Ayeka!

00:13:29.188 --> 00:13:30.022
Masayo!

00:13:30.022 --> 00:13:30.990
Ayeka!

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:34.926
There's some serious
female bonding starting here...

00:13:38.364 --> 00:13:40.958
It's him! Isao's shown up!

00:13:41.467 --> 00:13:42.568
Did you take him on?

00:13:42.568 --> 00:13:45.503
Yeah, but I didn't stand a chance.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:51.310
So the rumors about
this mysterious racer, Isao,

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:53.012
who blew in out of nowhere are true...

00:13:53.012 --> 00:13:55.378
I ain't never seen anybody
as amazing as that guy!

00:13:57.150 --> 00:14:00.253
Isao? Wait, don't tell me
he's the guy Masayo talked about?

00:14:00.253 --> 00:14:03.416
Huh? Sister? Masayo?

00:14:05.658 --> 00:14:07.627
Where's Isao?

00:14:07.627 --> 00:14:08.761
Who the hell are you?

00:14:08.761 --> 00:14:11.998
Where's Isao?!

00:14:11.998 --> 00:14:15.201
Ow! He's probably out of the area by now!

00:14:15.201 --> 00:14:18.728
He did five laps in the
time it took us to do one!

00:14:19.405 --> 00:14:20.895
Masayo!

00:14:23.142 --> 00:14:25.912
Hey, now, where do you think you're going?

00:14:25.912 --> 00:14:28.247
You can't leave without them, remember?

00:14:28.247 --> 00:14:30.183
But Isao... He's...

00:14:30.183 --> 00:14:34.453
Don't forget, you're a Guardian Spirit.

00:14:34.453 --> 00:14:37.990
You'll take them to Tokyo as soon
as possible, just as you were ordered.

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:39.091
Understand?

00:14:39.091 --> 00:14:40.593
Masayo!

00:14:40.593 --> 00:14:43.529
Got it? Don't forget your orders.

00:14:43.529 --> 00:14:46.632
Masayo! Masayo!

00:14:46.632 --> 00:14:48.463
Let's go to Tokyo.

00:14:50.636 --> 00:14:52.501
Sister...

00:14:56.342 --> 00:14:58.333
Huh? Something's coming!

00:15:00.947 --> 00:15:03.108
What's that noise?

00:15:04.717 --> 00:15:06.412
That sound, it's...

00:15:14.694 --> 00:15:15.795
Isao!

00:15:15.795 --> 00:15:17.597
Huh? That was him?

00:15:17.597 --> 00:15:19.332
I couldn't make anything out...

00:15:19.332 --> 00:15:21.400
I'd recognize him anywhere.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:24.733
He's the man I love more than anything.

00:15:26.272 --> 00:15:27.940
Hop in. I have to go to Tokyo.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.943
Huh? But why? Let's go after Isao!

00:15:30.943 --> 00:15:31.844
That's okay.

00:15:31.844 --> 00:15:35.181
No, it's not! You can't let the man
you love get away, not when he's...

00:15:35.181 --> 00:15:36.449
It's okay!

00:15:36.449 --> 00:15:39.485
I have to take you two to Tokyo.

00:15:39.485 --> 00:15:44.991
Yes, I certainly want to
have you drop us off in Tokyo.

00:15:44.991 --> 00:15:47.293
Sister!

00:15:47.293 --> 00:15:51.923
But I can see Lord Tenchi
whenever I'm in Tokyo.

00:15:52.898 --> 00:15:56.302
So let's chase after him, Masayo!

00:15:56.302 --> 00:15:57.603
But...

00:15:57.603 --> 00:16:01.440
To tell you the truth,
I'm scared of going to Tokyo.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:06.345
Of finding out how the man
I love, Lord Tenchi, really feels.

00:16:06.345 --> 00:16:10.116
When I think of that girl,
Sakuya, and Lord Tenchi,

00:16:10.116 --> 00:16:13.519
my body refuses to move.

00:16:13.519 --> 00:16:17.323
I think it's for the best
that I met you, Masayo.

00:16:17.323 --> 00:16:22.194
Now I know I'm not the
only one. So let's go after him.

00:16:22.194 --> 00:16:29.201
Give me courage by catching Isao!
The courage to chase the man I love!

00:16:29.201 --> 00:16:30.668
You got it!

00:16:46.719 --> 00:16:49.155
Let's go!

00:16:49.155 --> 00:16:50.816
Isao!

00:16:53.626 --> 00:16:55.719
- Huh?! That's Isao?!
- Huh?! That's Isao?!

00:16:59.098 --> 00:17:00.733
Why isn't he on a bike?!

00:17:00.733 --> 00:17:03.669
Running means everything to Isao!

00:17:03.669 --> 00:17:06.505
Isao! It's Masayo!

00:17:06.505 --> 00:17:09.642
It's no use! He's too focused on his running!

00:17:09.642 --> 00:17:12.634
There's no other choice, then,
Masayo! You have to beat him!

00:17:14.914 --> 00:17:16.782
Let's go!

00:17:16.782 --> 00:17:18.684
Go!

00:17:18.684 --> 00:17:22.120
Go! Go!

00:17:30.029 --> 00:17:32.898
It's hopeless! We're not
gaining any ground on him at all!

00:17:32.898 --> 00:17:35.301
But we're so close... What can we do?

00:17:35.301 --> 00:17:38.137
L-I can't take any more! Let me off!

00:17:38.137 --> 00:17:42.441
What are you saying? How can
you think of abandoning Masayo?!

00:17:42.441 --> 00:17:46.545
Right! If we get off, the bike will
be lighter and should go faster!

00:17:46.545 --> 00:17:48.180
Sasami! Ryo-Ohki! We're getting off!

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:50.616
Great! Let's get off! Let's get...

00:17:50.616 --> 00:17:51.817
Let's...

00:17:51.817 --> 00:17:53.285
How?!

00:17:53.285 --> 00:17:55.421
That's crazy!

00:17:55.421 --> 00:17:56.922
Let's do it, Masayo!

00:17:56.922 --> 00:17:58.685
Ayeka!

00:18:12.872 --> 00:18:14.100
Now!

00:18:15.508 --> 00:18:18.644
Isao! Isao! Isao! Isao! Isao!

00:18:18.644 --> 00:18:21.647
Isao! Isao! Isao! Isao!

00:18:21.647 --> 00:18:25.879
Isao! Isao!

00:18:27.453 --> 00:18:29.148
Masayo?

00:18:39.665 --> 00:18:41.267
We're saved...

00:18:41.267 --> 00:18:43.292
What about Masayo and Isao?

00:18:44.904 --> 00:18:46.038
Masayo!

00:18:46.038 --> 00:18:48.774
Ayeka... Sasami... Thank you.

00:18:48.774 --> 00:18:51.343
Now we can go back to the comet.

00:18:51.343 --> 00:18:53.004
Comet?

00:18:55.548 --> 00:18:58.484
Take care. Be happy.

00:18:58.484 --> 00:19:01.146
Goodbye. Thank you.

00:19:04.523 --> 00:19:06.616
Keep trying, Ayeka!

00:19:08.294 --> 00:19:14.233
I will! I'll find out how
Lord Tenchi really feels!

00:19:15.601 --> 00:19:18.504
So it wasn't a twin comet,
it was a lovers' comet.

00:19:18.504 --> 00:19:22.274
And why was the guy running?

00:19:22.274 --> 00:19:25.437
What was the point of
me making them riders?

00:19:30.549 --> 00:19:32.485
Where are we?

00:19:32.485 --> 00:19:34.520
Sendai, it says.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:39.184
What's Sendai? Where is Sendai?
Which way is Tokyo?!

00:19:41.427 --> 00:19:45.363
I guess we overshot
Tokyo when we were racing.

00:19:46.265 --> 00:19:48.234
Th-This is nothing to be discouraged about!

00:19:48.234 --> 00:19:51.437
If I have my love for Lord Tenchi,
I'll hitchhike anywhere,

00:19:51.437 --> 00:19:53.572
be it Sendai or even America!

00:19:53.572 --> 00:19:55.941
Are you ready, Sasami?!

00:19:55.941 --> 00:19:58.842
We're going to Tokyo!

00:20:03.883 --> 00:20:06.385
Well, I guess it's time to...

00:20:06.385 --> 00:20:09.047
Who could it be at this hour?

00:20:11.524 --> 00:20:15.461
A-Ayeka? Sasami?

00:20:15.461 --> 00:20:18.624
What happened to you two?

00:20:21.133 --> 00:20:23.727
Hey! Wait!

00:20:32.578 --> 00:20:35.172
They're finally back, huh?

00:20:38.717 --> 00:20:42.016
What the heck were they up to?

00:20:46.325 --> 00:20:49.021
Damn... All right, all right...

00:20:53.899 --> 00:20:57.300
I'll make you tell me all about it tomorrow.

00:21:00.539 --> 00:21:04.236
Masayo... Be happy...

00:21:35.741 --> 00:21:39.345
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:39.345 --> 00:21:43.248
<i>Sleeping late, staying up late,</i>
<i>and napping all the time!</i>

00:21:43.248 --> 00:21:46.852
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:46.852 --> 00:21:50.789
<i>Sneaking bites to eat, midnight</i>
<i>snacks, and pouring tea on my rice!</i>

00:21:50.789 --> 00:21:54.293
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:54.293 --> 00:21:58.263
<i>Playing video games and singing karaoke!</i>

00:21:58.263 --> 00:22:01.600
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:05.604
<i>Lying in the sun and taking baths outside!</i>

00:22:05.604 --> 00:22:07.740
<i>- Taking side trips!</i>
<i>- Gossiping!</i>

00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:09.675
<i>- Taking long baths</i>
<i>- Wasting my money!</i>

00:22:09.675 --> 00:22:11.176
<i>- Being a busybody!</i>
<i>- Talking forever on the phone!</i>

00:22:11.176 --> 00:22:17.016
<i>- Unrequited love!</i>
<i>- Stealing other people's men!</i>

00:22:17.016 --> 00:22:21.120
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it,</i>

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:24.390
<i>no matter how old I get!</i>

00:22:24.390 --> 00:22:27.926
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it,</i>

00:22:27.926 --> 00:22:32.625
<i>even if I die, change shape, or get reborn!</i>

00:22:42.174 --> 00:22:43.642
Tenchi Masaki here.

00:22:43.642 --> 00:22:47.946
Sakuya and her friends are running
a crêpes booth at the School Festival.

00:22:47.946 --> 00:22:49.782
I'll be helping out.

00:22:49.782 --> 00:22:53.218
But the girls are acting strange...

00:22:53.218 --> 00:22:56.221
Something is sneaking around in the shadows.

00:22:56.221 --> 00:23:03.929
And Amagasaki is acting even stranger
than usual. You don't suppose he...

00:23:03.929 --> 00:23:10.164
Next time on <i>Tenchi in Tokyo:</i>
"Love Match."
